        <item>
            <title>3.19.2</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:34:30 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>206</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>3.19.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Changes
- Worktrees opened through the control socket (`open_session` with `worktreeBranch`, e.g. from `canopyctl` or a bot) now get the repository's ignored files copied in, as the launcher already did, so build artifacts and `node_modules` are present and the new worktree can build. This works even when `cwd` is a subfolder of the repository.
- If some ignored files could not be copied, the `open_session` result includes a `seedWarning`.
- Creating and seeding the worktree no longer blocks the daemon while it runs.
]]></description>
